+# R46 / 0.1.33 — Bluetooth startup status and attempt isolation
+
+Baseline: R45 candidate based on R44 source artifact 15014496262 / commit 9bc86ce53237b83c23e588e6fa2c7376cca99381. The reported R44 log shows three RFCOMM connections, iAP2 link readiness and unverified MFi responses, then 0x4300 with no observed cumulative ACK, followed by fresh SYN and termination. It does not prove the receiver's reason for restarting.
+
+Changes:
+- Record RFCOMM establishment separately from iAP2 synchronization; record 0x4300 submission without implying local write, ACK or peer authorization.
+- Bluetooth milestone callbacks now carry the original timeline attempt ID and check the session lease. Late events cannot mark a replacement timeline as connected.
+- Localized progress and terminal status distinguish missing RFCOMM, unfinished iAP2 negotiation, and CarPlay startup/endpoint delivery. Historical evidence does not imply the socket remains online. Removed misleading authentication-success wording.
+- Use equivalent lambda and FIFO append syntax for the local Kotlin compiler.
+- No changes to authentication policy, on-wire messages, probe timings, or reconnect limits. No claim that E2LB now accepts 0x4300.
+
+Validation: 16 ConnectionProgressTest cases passed with standalone Kotlin/JVM, minimal JUnit-compatible harness and nonserializing JSONObject stub. This tests in-memory state, not Android resource packaging, Bluetooth callbacks on a device, or diagnostic JSON serialization. Chinese/English resource XML and referenced string IDs checked. Prior R45 51 transport tests are historical and not rerun in this round. Full Android build unavailable locally; no APK, no vehicle validation, no remote repository mutation.
